      <div type="clause" n="70.23">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 70.23</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 70.23" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="590" ed="#liebermann"/>Si mulier absque liberis moriatur, parentes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#Hn_70-23.lnote.oe.e"/> eius cum marito suo partem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Hn_70-23.lnote.oe.7"/> suam diuidant.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 590 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-23.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">590</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">angeborene Sippe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">kindred by birth</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-23.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">590</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. s. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. s. missing Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-23.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">In meisten German. Rechten, auch dem Englischen, hat der Mann kein gesetzliches Erbrecht am Nachlasse der Frau; Schröder <hi rend="italic">Ehel. Güterr</hi>. I 169.—71 <hi rend="italic">De h</hi>. ohne <hi rend="italic">mal</hi>.{9} Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In most Germanic laws, the English included, the husband has no legal right of inheritance to his wife’s estate; Schröder <hi rend="italic">Ehel. Güterr</hi>. I 169.—71 <hi rend="italic">De h</hi>. without <hi rend="italic">mal</hi>.{9} Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
